Subject: [PATCH] fleet: mirror fork patches to disk, document fleet workflow
 separately

Adds fleet-patches/*.patch (git format-patch mirror of every
fork-exclusive commit, plus a regenerate.sh script) so the patch set
survives without a live clone of the branch and a rebase conflict has
a static reference to work from. Previously these existed only as
commits on fleet-patches itself.

Adds FLEET.md (fork-only, doesn't exist upstream, zero rebase-conflict
risk) for operational knowledge that doesn't belong in AGENTS.md/
CLAUDE.md since those are shared verbatim with ggml-org/llama.cpp and
get replayed through every rebase. Documents the patch-mirror workflow
and the known-fragile draft-mtp+parallel+split-KV-cache area (two real
bugs already fixed there, a third -- MTP+grammar corruption -- found
today, not yet patched).

